      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While Vitamin C is an antioxidant, high-dose supplementation for kidney stones requires a very careful approach. For calcium oxalate stones, excessive Vitamin C can actually increase oxalate excretion, potentially worsening your stone formation risk. You should definitely discuss this with your nephrologist before starting any high-dose regimen to ensure it aligns with your specific stone chemistry and health profile.",
      "source": "target",
